WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.310
A new kind of café opens:

2
00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:05.840
bubble tea. Queues
stretch out of the door.

3
00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:08.030
The price of each drink is well above what

4
00:00:08.030 --> 00:00:09.470
it costs to make.

5
00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:12.020
The owner earns a big profit.

6
00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:14.830
A few years on, the drinks still sell.

7
00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:18.270
But now the shop only
just covers its costs.

8
00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:20.520
Nobody stopped buying bubble tea.

9
00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.220
So where did the big profit go?

10
00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:25.830
In this mission, you'll
find the price and output

11
00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:28.230
that give this café the most profit.

12
00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:30.950
Then you'll change the
market in a graph lab,

13
00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:33.970
and predict where each shop
ends up in the long run.

14
00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:37.320
Your mission: find out
why big early profits can

15
00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:39.470
shrink to just covering costs.
